BT /F2 9 Tf 0 0.39 0.46 rg 47 764 Td (Shared Values, Shared Purpose) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.7 Tf 0 0.392 0.455 rg 47 720.0 Td (2. Shared values are not identical political positions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 697.9 Td (De Jong argues that coordination on paper can break down when organizations do not examine the values beneath) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 684.7 Td (their choices. One group may prioritize access and flexibility, another strict program rules; one may invite) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 671.5 Td (lived-experience testimony without letting that input affect decisions. The result can be contradictory messages) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 658.3 Td (and fragmented help.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 639.1 Td (For this community event, the first agreement is more basic: everyone deserves dignity, safety, an opportunity to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 625.9 Td (be heard, and an honest conversation. Participants can disagree about specific policies without dehumanizing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 612.7 Td (neighbors or one another.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 593.5 Td (Awareness doesn't take sides ... all voices and perspectives are encouraged. That welcome does not mean that) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 580.3 Td (Campout has no position about the materials it recommends. Respectful participation is open; editorial selection of) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 567.1 Td (resources remains with the project.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.7 Tf 0 0.392 0.455 rg 47 538.9 Td (3. Twelve values to begin the conversation) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 516.8 Td (The following is a concise, locally adapted summary of De Jong's twelve proposed values, kept in the order of his) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 503.6 Td (video. He presents them as conversation starters, not commandments. They can be discussed without asking every) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 490.4 Td (host to endorse all twelve.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 471.2 Td (1. Housing is a human right. A safe, stable home should not depend on someone first proving readiness or meeting) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 458.0 Td (preconditions. Discuss: What would it mean for a neighbor to have a genuinely workable path to housing?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 438.8 Td (2. Lived experience means co-design, not tokenism. People who have experienced homelessness should shape decisions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 425.6 Td (and evaluation, not simply be invited to tell their story. Discuss: Whose input changes the plans we make?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 406.4 Td (3. Voluntary engagement and autonomy matter. Services should meet people where they are and respect individual) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 393.2 Td (choice. Discuss: How can we offer help without taking away dignity or agency?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 374.0 Td (4. Support, not surveillance. Assistance should not mean control of a person's every move. Discuss: When do program) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 360.8 Td (rules support stability, and when do they become barriers?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 341.6 Td (5. Cultural safety and equity matter. Different communities face unequal risks and barriers; inclusion needs more) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 328.4 Td (than a generic invitation. Discuss: Who might feel excluded from our gathering or our services?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 309.2 Td (6. Trauma-informed care is foundational. Safety, trust, and avoiding re-traumatization belong in the design of help.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 296.0 Td (Discuss: How do we make listening and participation safe?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 276.8 Td (7. Progressive engagement. Begin with the lightest support that works and increase assistance according to need) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 263.6 Td (and interest. Discuss: What does it look like to offer help without demanding a test of worthiness?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 244.4 Td (8. Build on strengths. Recognize capabilities, relationships, resilience, and potential rather than reducing someone) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 231.2 Td (to problems. Discuss: What strengths are commonly overlooked?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 212.0 Td (9. Provide non-judgmental service. Curiosity and compassion open doors that blame can close. Discuss: How can we ask) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 198.8 Td (questions without assuming a person's story?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 179.6 Td (10. Use data for people, not against them. Information should improve outcomes and inform decisions, not become a) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 166.4 Td (means of gatekeeping. Discuss: Which numbers actually show whether someone became more stable?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 147.2 Td (11. Recovery is not linear. Setbacks, missed appointments, and relapses need not end a person's opportunity for) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 134.0 Td (support. Discuss: How should a community respond when progress is uneven?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 114.8 Td (12. Keep moving toward housing. Services and policies should be assessed by whether they contribute to housing) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.8 Tf 0.14 0.20 0.27 rg 47 101.6 Td (outcomes. Discuss: Are we making homelessness less visible, or helping people become housed?) Tj ET
